    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0486" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">111.70Am3/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-26T20:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1919,
                                8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 28,
                            1.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>For Ely, War Trade Board.</p>
                <p>Arrived Saturday, was presented to President Bertrand [yesterday] by Minister and
                    the President has already in response to my suggestion that he designate a
                    lawyer to work with me named Alberto Rodriguez apparently a suitable choice.
                    There is a fair prospect of adequate action. Please cable me immediately
                    regarding any defects in Guatemalan enactments<anchor n="23" xml:id="d358-f1"/>
                    which it would be well to remedy in Honduranean law. Ames.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d358-f1" n="23" xml:id="d358-f1-content">
                <p>See despatch No. 18, Feb. 24, from the Special Agent of the Department, <ref
                        target="#pg289">p. 289</ref>.</p>
            </note>
